 "result": "The default session (`SignedCookieSessionInterface`) serializes its cookie payload with a tagged JSON serializer.\n\n- **`src/tessel/sessions.py`**:\n  - `SignedCookieSessionInterface` sets `serializer = session_json_serializer`, a module-level `TypedCookieSerializer()` instance.\n  - It passes that serializer into the signing serializer for the cookie (around line 316).\n  - `SignedCookieSession` is the session object itself.\n- **`src/tessel/json/tag.py`**:\n  - `TypedCookieSerializer` (line 219) runs the tagging on `dumps` and untagging on `loads`.\n  - `TypeMarker` (line 60) is the base class. Each subclass checks for a Python type, converts it to a JSON-safe form under a one-key tag dict, and converts it back on load.\n  - `TagTuple` handles tuples.\n  - `TagBytes` handles bytes.\n  - `TagDateTime` handles datetimes.\n  - `TagDict`, `PassDict` and `PassList` handle dicts and lists that would otherwise be mistaken for tags.\n  - `TagMarkup` and `TagUUID` handle markup and UUIDs.\n\nI haven't read the method bodies, so the exact tag keys and ordering are not confirmed.",
